<h2 id="code-400-version-missing">400 VERSION_MISSING · A version must be present · no Linkedin-Version header</h2>
<p><strong>What it means.</strong> The call reached a versioned LinkedIn endpoint with no <code>Linkedin-Version</code> header. This often shows up after moving from the old <code>ugcPosts</code> API to <code>/rest/posts</code>, which LinkedIn says replaces it.</p>
<p><strong>How to fix it.</strong> Add <code>Linkedin-Version: 202610</code> and <code>X-Restli-Protocol-Version: 2.0.0</code> to every request to <code>https://api.linkedin.com/rest/</code>. LinkedIn's Posts API page says all of its APIs require both headers.</p>
<p><strong>Through Siar.</strong> You will not see this code. Siar sets both headers on every call.</p>
<CodeBlock title="LinkedIn's documented response for a missing header" code={r400} lang="json" />
